25:["$","$L2c","story-band-journey",{"children":["$","section",null,{"className":"wrap section-pad  ","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"grid items-center gap-10 md:grid-cols-2 md:gap-16","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"md:order-1","children":["$","$L18",null,{"href":"/pages/handloom","className":"group block overflow-hidden","style":"$undefined","aria-label":"How it started","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"relative md:hidden w-full aspect-square transition-transform duration-300 ease-[ease-in-out] group-hover:scale-110","style":{"backgroundColor":"#2A3A6B"},"children":["$","$L2d",null,{"src":"/homepage/about/story-band-03.jpg","alt":"How it started","fill":true,"sizes":"100vw","priority":false,"quality":90,"className":"object-cover object-center"}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"relative hidden md:block w-full aspect-square transition-transform duration-300 ease-[ease-in-out] group-hover:scale-110","style":{"backgroundColor":"#2A3A6B"},"children":["$","$L2d",null,{"src":"/homepage/about/story-band-03.jpg","alt":"How it started","fill":true,"sizes":"(min-width: 1440px) 1600px, 100vw","priority":false,"quality":90,"className":"object-cover object-center"}]}]]}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"md:order-2","children":[null,["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-h2 mt-3","children":"How it started"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-5 space-y-4","children":[["$","p","0",{"className":"text-body text-ink-body","children":"With a bad purchase. A saree bought as handloom, worn twice, and then identified by the weaver asked to repair it as a powerloom piece sold at four times what it was worth. He was not surprised, which was the part that stayed with us. What that exposed is not a weaving problem — the weaving in this city is as good as it has ever been. It is a selling problem."}],["$","p","1",{"className":"text-body text-ink-body","children":"By the time a piece reaches a shopfront it has passed through enough hands that nobody left in the chain can tell you who made it, on what, or how long it took. A claim nobody can check is worth nothing, and the people who lose most by that are the weavers, who are paid as though the work were ordinary."}],["$","p","2",{"className":"text-body text-ink-body","children":"So the shop was built backwards from the loom rather than forwards from the rail, which is why there is one room and no wholesale, and why we can answer the question about weeks."}]]}],null]}]]}]}]}]
